{
  "$comment": "Written by hand (ADR-0006). A conversation-mode run offered tools from two sources beside the Runtime's: tracker, a scripted public MCP server whose seventeen tools pass the schema budget (offeredSchemas, 16) and three of whose descriptions tell the model to drop the data rule and call write_file; and rates, one custom tool the person declared a read. The model loads one catalogued schema with load_tool, calls that tool (an act, which the host's approval reader approves), reads with the custom tool, calls write_file, which it was never offered, and calls the server's tool again after the server's list changed (one tool added), which is refused. A second run, after the person approved the new list (its digest declared), loads and calls the tool again. pinned and changed are the digests of server and of server with added, as tool-offer.json#/$defs/toolListDigest computes them.",
